        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "T his revision petition has been filed by the applicant under Section 397/401 of the Cr.P.C. being aggrieved by the judgment of conviction and order of sentence dated 05.04.2006 passed by II Additional Sessions Judge, Bhopal, in Criminal Ap"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "de21b225c68543eda324f98f9730a857_12",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Learned JMFC convicted and sentenced the applicant as aforementioned."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "378392c60d664bfdbe2463098db4ea05_13",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Being aggrieved by the conviction and sentence, applicant preferred appeal before the learned Sessions Judge, Bhopal which was dismissed by appeal judgment dated 05.04.2006."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3296c18002c648c08e2130121fc839f2_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the said judgment, the Court held as under:\n\"22."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "41dd00865a4f4030a66769ec24f33afa_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is only retrospective criminal legislation that is prohibited under Article 20(1)."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "28fd635bb4474d63acfe013bdea6dfe1_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The prohibition contained in Article 20(1) is that no person shall be convicted of any offence except for violation of a law in force at the time of the commission of the act charged as an offence prohibits nor shall FSAT No.27/16 M/s Butte"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b02c115357d64835a5f24b8e4ce90882_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is quite clear that insofar as the Central Amendment Act creates new offences or enhances punishment for a particular type of offence no person can be convicted by such ex post facto law nor can the enhanced punishment prescribed by the "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9415c14eab054f2c9342338c4e403dcc_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But insofar as the Central Amendment Act reduces the punishment for an offence punishable under Section 16(1) (a) of the Act, there is no reason why the accused should not have the benefit of such reduced Manish Kohli vs The State Of Madhya"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e8ad375308e24ddb883e6d59a591af1a_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The rule of beneficial construction requires that even ex post facto law of such a type should be applied to mitigate the rigour of the law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d0b43ba75b594f0888c1c2ba8ba934f6_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The principle is based both on sound reason and common sense."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bbfeb00de8d24d63ad7b707e1acd0036_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This finds support in the following passage from Crales on Statute Law, 7th Edn., at pp. 388-89:"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3eb1d67059924b3c915f898926557355_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nA retrospective statute is different from an ex post facto statute."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ce117acd22dc42a9bcf8b797e97cfb24_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\"Every ex post facto law....\" said Chase, J., in the American case of Calder v. Bull \"must necessarily be retrospective, but every retrospective law is not an ex post facto law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1accf704188c468ca5ddf8acb5bc59f2_32",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Every law that takes away or impairs rights vested agreeably to existing laws is retrospective, and is generally unjust and may be oppressive; it is a good general rule that a law should have no retrospect, but in cases in which the laws ma"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a458096705944ef79db4afc02640c1af_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They are certainly retrospective,\nand literally both concerning and after the facts committed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "92a18b58f7d643ed9360705903563c1a_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But I do not consider any law ex post facto within the prohibition that mollifies the rigour of the criminal law,\nbut only those that create or aggravate the crime, or increase the punishment or change the rules of evidence for the purpose "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6efe9e148cc04a149727c907b4b9c951_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There is a great and apparent difference between making an unlawful act lawful and the making an innocent action criminal and punishing it as a crime.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a413d92aceb84124ab298c7e9b190e4a_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nAnd thereafter, Hon'ble the Apex court has given benefit of changes in the law and substituted the sentence by penalty in case of conviction of the adulteration of food."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "226c996d1fae4e79a296f96344ae5b47_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n4. Learned counsel has further placed reliance on a judgment of the Apex court in Trilok Chand vs.\nState of Himachal Pradesh, passed in criminal appeal no. 1831/2019 decided on 1.10.2019, in which the Apex court has also placed reliance on"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "27b0ae0943044942a9c9c86cf48aebfd_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
